-- title:
--   Toricity of p-new finite points up to a bounded multiple
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, together with a proof $h_{pN_0}$ that $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbf{Q}$ satisfying `LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with a structure morphism $f$ to `base p`, a relative group law $L$ on $f$ over `baseRing p`, and bijections identifying `JZero N₀` with the sections of $f$ over the generic point and `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` with the sections over the residue point. Assume $h_\Lambda \colon \Lambda$.`IsJacobian`, the conjunction asserting that $f$ carries the abelian-scheme property bundle, that $L$ is commutative, that both point bijections are additive, that `pts` is Galois-equivariant, that reduction of points agrees mod $\ell$ whenever the relevant inputs hold, and that every Hecke operator is induced by an endomorphism of $f$ over `base p`. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`: a scheme $G$ over `base p` with a relative group law whose sections over the generic point are identified additively, Galois- and Hecke-equivariantly with `JZero (N₀ * p)`, which is smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact and surjective with preconnected fibres, whose multiplication-by-$n$ maps are flat and surjective for $n > 0$, whose generic fibre is proper, and which carries a toric rank together with further data. The conclusion: there exists $c \in \mathbf{N}$ with $c > 0$, independent of $m$, such that for every $m > 0$ and every $x$ in $O$.`finPts m` — the subgroup of `JZero (N₀ * p)` generated by those $m$-torsion classes whose associated point under $O$.`pts` extends to a place over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ — if both degeneracy pushforwards $x \mapsto$ `degeneracyPushforwardPair N₀ p 0 x` and `degeneracyPushforwardPair N₀ p 1 x` (the two homomorphisms `JZero (N₀ * p) → JZero N₀` given by pushforward of degree-zero divisor classes along the two degeneracy maps, and zero if the required inputs fail) vanish, then $c \cdot x$ lies in $O$.`toricPts m`, the subgroup generated by the range of the toric points at level $m$.
--
--   This is Ribet's exact sequence at finite level in the form needed here: on the $m$-torsion of the finite part, the kernel of the pair of degeneracy pushforwards (the $p$-new condition) is contained in the toric subgroup after multiplication by one fixed positive integer, uniformly in $m$ and including $p$-power levels. It feeds the construction of the ordinary Néron data at $p$ and the bounds on the monodromy span inside the eigenplane of the Tate module attached to a newform.
